        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the number of whole numbers less than 100 that are divisible by 2 or 3, or both.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$67$",
          "worked": "The whole numbers are $0$ to $99$. Include $0$, since $0\\div2=0$ and $0\\div3=0$.\n\nMultiples of $2$: $0,2,\\ldots,98$, giving $50$ numbers.\n\nMultiples of $3$: $0,3,\\ldots,99$, giving $34$ numbers.\n\nNumbers divisible by both are multiples of $6$: $0,6,\\ldots,96$, giving $17$ numbers. Subtract these once because they were counted twice.\n\n$$50+34-17=67.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p27-q13-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": {
