        "answer": {
          "short": "$167$",
          "worked": "There are $500$ whole numbers from $0$ to $499$.\n\nMultiples of $2$: $0,2,\\ldots,498$, giving $250$ numbers.\n\nMultiples of $3$: $0,3,\\ldots,498$, giving $167$ numbers.\n\nMultiples of both are multiples of $6$: $0,6,\\ldots,498$, giving $84$ numbers.\n\nThe number divisible by $2$ or $3$ is $250+167-84=333$.\n\nThe number divisible by neither is $500-333=167$.",
